= Coup in Cyprus!

News have reached Ankara that a coup led by the far right EOKA-B and supported by the Nationalist Greek Junta has taken place in Cyprus on July 15th, days after president Archbishop Makarios's letter to the Junta calling the Greek troops to be retreated from the island and the Junta's ceasing of assasination attempts against Makarios's life.

It's reported that at midnight armed Greek militias raided the presidential palace and took over the Cypriot government. At a press conference in the morning, the head of the new Cypriot Junta Nikos Sampson announced the death of Makarios and the reallocation of the presidential seat. Luckily though, it turned out that Makarios managed to survive by escaping through the back door of the palace and has declared the Cypriot Junta null from London.

The conflict between the two sides arose largely due to their attitude in regard to ENOSIS, the unification of Cyprus with Greece. While both Makarios and the ultranationalists in EOKA-B supported the idea of ENOSIS, Makarios supported a more gradual integration and viewed the far right Greek Junta as unreliable. The supporters of EOKA-B however support a much swifter and crueler stance: ENOSIS shall be reached **now**, even if it requires the ethnic cleansing of the Turks on the island. Once they deal with the last remnants of the supporters of Makarios, it's more than likely that they will unleash even greater horrors upon the Turkish Cypriots.

And thus the prospect of intervention on the island is growing more and more as time passes. Rauf Denktaş has reported through telegram that 'this is the last chance Turkey will get to intervene' and if we stall or fail, there may not be a Turkish population left to save.

Time slows, and we enter the day by day struggle.
  
- @root: The War for Peace...

